Id: pass013w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_passwd
Fix: Set ENCRYPT_METHOD SHA512 (or YESCRYPT) in login.defs and have the password reset.
References: login.defs(5); crypt(5)
Controls: CIS 5.2; NIST IA-5(1), SC-13; ISO 5.17, 8.24; CE User access control

The listed username is not using an acceptable, cryptographic method for the
password hash.

Acceptable, unless Tigris_Passwd_Hashes says otherwise, are yescrypt,
gost-yescrypt, scrypt, bcrypt, sha512crypt and sha256crypt (and the SM3
ones). DES crypt (crypt3: only the first 8 characters of the password
count) and md5crypt are reported, as are the other legacy formats
crypt(5) lists (sha1crypt, sunmd5, nt, bsdicrypt, bcrypt's $2x$): all
are fast enough to search for the password on one GPU. A hash in a
format Tigris does not recognise is reported as such rather than taken
for a locked account: it may be one the system accepts. Only ! or * in
front of the hash means locked.

Changing ENCRYPT_METHOD affects passwords set from then on; each
account's password must be set again (passwd, or chpasswd) for its hash
to change.
